      "pins": ["SW6.1", "SW6.2", "SW6.3", "SW6.4", "R34.1", "R34.2", "R35.1", "R35.2"],
      "nets": ["/CAN0_P", "/CAN0_N", "/CAN1_P", "/CAN1_N", "Net-(R34-Pad2)", "Net-(R35-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "SW6 is a two-circuit DIP switch. Its first switch connects the far ends of R34 and R35, which are otherwise on /CAN0_N and /CAN1_N; its second switch connects /CAN1_P and /CAN0_P. Thus, closing the switches couples the two CAN buses instead of independently terminating each bus across its own P/N pair.",
      "expected": "Keep CAN0 and CAN1 electrically independent. If SW6 is intended to select termination, each switch should connect a 120-ohm resistor across the corresponding bus's P and N nets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/CAN0_P\") ... (node (ref \"SW6\") (pin \"4\")) ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"7\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/CAN1_P\") ... (node (ref \"SW6\") (pin \"3\")) ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"7\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/CAN0_N\") ... (node (ref \"R34\") (pin \"1\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/CAN1_N\") ... (node (ref \"R35\") (pin \"1\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(R34-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"SW6\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(R35-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"SW6\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Closing the switches can couple the two nominally isolated CAN interfaces, causing bus interference or communication failures; the resistors also do not provide the expected independent P-to-N termination.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomaly detected: SW6's wiring couples the two CAN buses when its switches are closed, rather than providing independent termination for CAN0 and CAN1. This conflicts with the specified separate, isolated CAN interfaces."
}

